      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!}\\), we will follow a step-by-step approach.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression in a more manageable form. Recall that \\((N+1)! = (N+1) \\cdot N!\\). So, we can substitute this into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!} = \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!}\n\\]\n\nNext, we can simplify the fraction by canceling out the common factor \\(N!\\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!} = \\frac{(N-1)! \\cdot N}{(N+1) \\cdot N!} = \\frac{N}{(N+1) \\cdot N! / (N-1)!}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(N! = N \\cdot (N-1)!\\), we can simplify the expression further:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{N}{(N+1) \\cdot N! / (N-1)!} = \\frac{N}{(N+1) \\cdot N \\cdot (N-1)! / (N-1)!} = \\frac{N}{(N+1) \\cdot N} = \\frac{1}{N+1}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{N+1}}\n\\]",
