    "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!}\\), we will first simplify the factorial terms in the numerator and the denominator.\n\nThe factorial \\((N+1)!\\) can be expanded as:\n\\[\n(N+1)! = (N+1) \\cdot N!\n\\]\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!} = \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!}\n\\]\nWe can cancel out \\(N!\\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!} = \\frac{(N-1)! \\cdot N}{(N+1) \\cdot N!} = \\frac{(N-1)! \\cdot N}{(N+1) \\cdot N \\cdot (N-1)!}\n\\]\nThe \\((N-1)!\\) terms cancel out:\n\\[\n\\frac{(N-1)! \\cdot N}{(N+1) \\cdot N \\cdot (N-1)!} = \\frac{N}{(N+1) \\cdot N} = \\frac{1}{N+1}\n\\]\nThus, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{N+1}}\n\\]",
